From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:38:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] d/steamvr_lh: resolve skeletal root through controller pose history

Skeletal samples retain a hand_pose captured when the skeleton was updated.
Predicting this root independently of the controller relation history can
produce a different global root for hand joints and their controller base
space. In WiVRn, controller prediction also follows LH_MAX_EXTRAPOLATION_MS,
which the skeletal root previously bypassed.

Resolve the returned hand_pose through Device::get_pose at the requested time,
so both paths share controller history and prediction policy. Keep local joint
poses, radii and output timestamps unchanged. No smoothing or diagnostics.

Based on WiVRn's pinned Monado plus existing patches 0001-0012. Tested diagnostic
equivalent at clamp=0 ms: wrist probe and VRChat fly-out resolved by user report.
Nonzero-clamp behavior remains outside this validation.

---
 src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp b/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
@@ -772,6 +772,10 @@
 		*out_timestamp_ns = desired_timestamp_ns;
 	}
 
+	// Resolve the skeletal root through the same history and prediction policy
+	// as the controller pose used as the base space for hand joints.
+	Device::get_pose(desired_timestamp_ns, &out_value->hand_pose);
+
 	return XRT_SUCCESS;
 }
 
